A competent operator should be able to:
•	 recognize whether or not the animals are in good health;
•	 understand the significance of a change in the behaviour of the animals;
•	 know when veterinary treatment is required;
•	 implement a planned herd health management programme, such as preventive treat-
ments or vaccination programmes when necessary;
•	 implement appropriate animal feeding and grassland management programmes;
•	 recognize if the general environment (indoors or outdoors) is adequate to promote 
good health and welfare;
•	 have management skills appropriate to the scale and technical requirements of the 
production system;
•	 handle animals compassionately and in an appropriate manner; and
•	 anticipate potential problems and take the necessary preventive action.
